#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Archive Supabase rows to R2 before they leave the database.

Rule of the project: nothing collected is discarded. Rows are written to the
private backups bucket (gzip JSONL plus a manifest), downloaded back and
checked (sha256 and row count), and only then cleared or deleted in the
database, after the database still matches the manifest.

Tables (one object per day, America/Sao_Paulo):
  consultas      after 7 days, clear api_response (the copy of
                 placa_cache.payload that nothing reads).
  api_chamadas   after 30 days, summarize the day (api_chamadas_resumir) and
                 delete the raw rows, except the paid sources wdapi and
                 placafipe that the fin reads.
  eventos_funil  after 30 days, summarize the day (eventos_funil_resumir:
                 eventos_funil_diario and funil_diario_arquivo) and delete the
                 raw rows.
  placa_cache    "podar": archive, then delete the cache rows past their use:
                 not found and older than 6 hours (the code ignores them), and
                 found but older than 90 days, except plates with a paid order
                 (the report reads their engine number). A plate that comes
                 back is fetched again.

Usage:
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> arquivar --dia 2026-08-03
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> arquivar --de 2026-08-03 --ate 2026-11-19 [--pausa 10]
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> liberar --ate 2026-11-11 [--vacuum-a-cada 10] [--confirmar]
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> diario [--confirmar]
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> status
  pc-supabase-arquivar placa_cache podar [--limite 5000] [--confirmar]

"liberar" clears the column (consultas) or summarizes and deletes (the
others); "zerar" is kept as its alias. Options: --ref <project ref> (default
prod), --prefixo <R2 prefix>. Without --confirmar, liberar and diario only
print what they would do. --vacuum-a-cada N runs a plain VACUUM of the table
after every N released days, so the next days reuse the space of the dead
rows instead of growing the files before the VACUUM FULL.
"""
